          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "आसीस (āsīs) goes back to Sanskrit āśis, \"a wish, a prayer; a blessing\" (CDIAL 1457; Monier-Williams). CDIAL gives no Marwari form in this entry, and no other modern form either: the Marwadi word keeps the Sanskrit shape, with स for श. It is feminine, and an elder gives it: आसीस देवै है."
